# Providhy ↔ Radian Design System

There is **no separate Providhy design system**. **Radian is the design system.**

**Radian design system = this exact Figma file** (Design System ❖ Version 0.3), published as a library:

`https://www.figma.com/design/TQngn3b7a4jlu8xD6SZiod/Design-System-%E2%9D%96-Version-0.3--Community-`

File key: `TQngn3b7a4jlu8xD6SZiod`

The **Providhy working file** (`ea33mdznzR2oa70arYuvT6` / “New”) is a **separate** Figma file that **consumes** that published library. Do **not** recreate or duplicate Radian inside the Providhy file. Use the published library for all Providhy pages.

**Product sources (Figma phase):** codebase = this repo (`https://github.com/RamKatwal/Multibranch`); live UI = `https://multibranch-kohl.vercel.app/`. Do **not** refactor code in the Figma phase — establish Figma first; code will follow later.

## Before creating any page

1. Inspect available Radian library components.
2. Identify the appropriate Radian component for each UI need.
3. Use **instances** of published Radian components.
4. Use available Radian **variants**.
5. Use Radian **variables/tokens** where available.
6. Do **not** create duplicate versions of existing Radian components.

## Design language (always)

Follow Radian typography (Geist; Heading/Body), spacing, colors, border radius, states/interaction patterns, and layout conventions. No arbitrary styling.

## If something is missing

Create a **Providhy-specific** component only when Radian has no match — smallest possible, built from Radian’s visual language and primitives. Prefer a new Radian variant in the library when that is the right long-term home; never fork a lookalike inside Providhy.

## Do not

- Copy the Radian design system into the Providhy file
- Invent a parallel Providhy component library or token set
- Hard-code one-off colors, type, radii, or shadows outside Radian tokens
- Duplicate Radian components under a Providhy name when an instance/variant would work
